# name: The keeper’s log
The logbook lies open at the last page. The hand is the keeper’s, and it gets worse as it goes.
"The fourteenth. Wind north-east, rising. The can in the lamp room is near dry. The full ones are in the store, and the store key is in my chest, where it always is." # speaker: keeper
"The fifteenth. The supply boat hasn’t come. The Mary Dunn is due before dawn on the sixteenth, and she won’t see the rock without the light." # speaker: keeper
"I’ll row across for the doctor. Back by dark." # speaker: keeper
* [Close the logbook.]
  # fx: set-flag(flag: read-log, to: true)
  Nobody has written since. It is long past dark.
-> END
